3. Use of super Keyword
The super keyword is used to access parent class constructors, methods and fields.

Java Program:

class Vehicle {
    String vehicleNo;

    Vehicle(String vehicleNo) {
        this.vehicleNo = vehicleNo;
        System.out.println("Vehicle Constructor");
    }
}

class Car extends Vehicle {
    int seats;

    Car(String vehicleNo, int seats) {
        super(vehicleNo);
        this.seats = seats;
        System.out.println("Car Constructor");
    }
}

class ElectricCar extends Car {
    int batteryCapacity;

    ElectricCar(String vehicleNo, int seats, int battery) {
        super(vehicleNo, seats);
        this.batteryCapacity = battery;
        System.out.println("ElectricCar Constructor");
    }
}

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ElectricCar e = new ElectricCar("TN01AB1234", 5, 60);
    }
}



4. Constructor Execution Order
When an ElectricCar object is created, constructors execute from the parent class to the child class.

